   "notes": "Bishop's Hostel, Trinity (1669-71): red brick with stone quoins, window surrounds and band course; two storeys of stone-mullioned leaded cross windows plus attic dormers in a tiled hipped roof; centre with giant stone pilasters and pediment over a panelled doorcase, flanked by gabled end wings. Commons view is elevated and oblique; matched to this 38 m wall by footprint orientation only, bay positions spread evenly. (length 38.0 m, height 10.0 m from walls.json)"
